    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8200cf73_be752fbd",
        "filename": "acme/autocert/autocert.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 253,
      "author": {
        "id": 6347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-11T23:43:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, that\u0027s because ServeHTTP doesn\u0027t need to wait for a certificate to be issued, it\u0027s only for cache and host policy. GetCertificate, in addition to caching and host policy, also needs to verify the domain and create a new certificate in the worst-case scenario.\n\nI only added some comments for now, but maybe 5min in GetCertificate is too long indeed. I haven\u0027t really done any useful measurements.",
      "parentUuid": "e95c4947_b4fcd5ab",
